body='''<div class="page-intro"><div class="eyebrow">Subdivision gate v0.1 · development</div><h1>Three conditions. One declared metric.</h1><p class="lede">The source subdivision map preserves boundaries, but norm preservation and generator compatibility are separate tests. A new conditional metric can satisfy all three while retaining the extra fine coordinates.</p></div><aside class="callout"><strong>Exact conditional construction · source selection open</strong><p>The extension changes the post-event pairing and its adjoint. It preserves the earlier Euclidean no-go result. Constructor-team checks do not supply independent human review or a physical bridge. Physical promotion 0.</p></aside>
<section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">01</div><div><h2>Inspect each transfer contract</h2><p>Ordinary barycentric subdivision maps15 chain coordinates to149. Its degree squared norm factors are1,2,6,24. A universal √2 scaling does not normalize this map.</p><div class="search-tools"><label>Declared branch<select id="sg-branch"><option value="ordinary">Ordinary source map · unit metric</option><option value="bounded">Bounded source map · S/√24</option><option value="degree">Normalize each degree separately</option><option value="diagonal">Compensate with diagonal degree metric</option><option value="retraction" selected>Retraction/complement metric · conditional</option></select></label></div><p id="sg-verdict" role="status"></p><div id="sg-conditions"></div><p id="sg-factors"></p><p>Generator defect values use the stated pairing. They are not endpoint-error bounds. The full proofs retain each branch's separate assumptions.</p></div></section>
<section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">02</div><div><h2>A coarse retraction supplies the missing structure</h2><p>Let S subdivide an oriented simplex into its signed barycentric flags. Define R by mapping each new face-vertex to the average of its original vertices and extending through exterior products. Exactly, RS=I and RB′=BR. With Q=I−SR, every fine chain splits into S(Rx)+Qx.</p><div class="callout"><p class="form">H=RᵀGR+QᵀWQ, with positive G and W</p><p>The new squared norm is the old decoded norm plus the retained complement norm. It is positive definite and gives SᵀHS=G. Using the correct H-adjoint also gives A′H S=S A_G.</p></div><p>The old15-coordinate evolution is therefore preserved on its embedded image, at the same internal rate. The full149-coordinate operator still has134 complementary directions. This is an authored compatibility construction; the sources do not select its metric or coarse readout.</p></div></section>
<section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">03</div><div><h2>What the metric change costs</h2><p>The metric generally has cross terms within each degree. Individual simplex squares no longer add to the total norm, so the original local stock/current rules cannot be carried over by name. A source law for locality, metric weights and measurement remains open.</p><p>The134 extra directions form a direct-sum chain complement. They are not134 qubits or a tensor donor bank. A complete transfer retains arbitrary complement information. Preparing zero complement amplitude, supplying the transfer clock and preserving outgoing records need their own implementation and resource accounting.</p><p>Exact singleton coefficients survive on the admitted coarse image; arbitrary fine states require a declared decoded observation. No free reset, indefinitely funded refinement, physical energy or spacetime identification follows.</p></div></section>
<section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">04</div><div><h2>Where √2 actually appears</h2><p>It is the edge case of the factorial norm factors. The rectangle's rotated-halving fixed point, equal-amplitude two-channel normalization and the K+ carrier frequency √2 are separately typed statements. They supply no universal kinetic/potential coupling or saturation ceiling.</p><p>Next: derive the source rule selecting a metric/retraction and a local observable, or retain the original metric and explicitly account for an interface generator defect. The finite-window clock, memory, output and reset obligations remain in force.</p></div></section><noscript><p>The branch inspector requires JavaScript. The proof and replay include every condition and negative control.</p></noscript><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/releases/UD_SUBDIVISION_THREE_CONDITION_GATE_v0.1.zip" download>Download subdivision proofs and replay ↓</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/subdivision-v0.1/UD_SUBDIVISION_THREE_CONDITION_GATE_v0.1.md">Theorems and proof</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/subdivision-v0.1/SUBDIVISION_METRIC_ROOT_VERIFICATION_v0.1.json">Exact root receipt</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/subdivision-v0.1/subdivision-metric-source-review.md">AI source/scope review</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/subdivision-v0.1/subdivision-metric-parallel-proof.md">Parallel proof and limits</a><a class="text-link" href="/dependencies/?node=SG-NEXT">Inspect dependencies</a><a class="text-link" href="/metric-admission/">Metric convention and spectral gates</a></div>'''
